| Description = '''[[Bruce Wayne (Prime Earth)|Batman]]''' is the super-hero protector of [[Gotham City]], a man dressed like a bat who fights against evil and strikes terror into the hearts of criminals everywhere. His civilian identity is '''Bruce Wayne''', billionaire industrialist and notorious playboy; and orphan following the sudden death of his parents by gunshot in [[Crime Alley]] by [[Joe Chill]].

Although Batman possesses no superhuman powers, he is one of the world's smartest men and one of its greatest fighters. His physical prowess and technical ingenuity make him an incredibly dangerous opponent. He is also a founding member of the [[Justice League]] and the [[Outsiders]]. Batman fights with a wide range of sidekicks and partners such as [[Robin]] and [[Batgirl]].

There have been times in which the mantle of Batman have been passed on and used by others; these people are:
* '''[[Jean-Paul Valley]]''', a.k.a. [[Azrael]], who took on the mantle following Batman's back breakage by Bane in the ''[[Batman: Knightfall|Knightfall]]'' crossover event. He was forcefully removed from the mantle by Bruce following his increasingly extreme methods of violence.
* '''[[Dick Grayson]]''', who first temporarily took on the mantle following Jean-Paul Valley being ousted from the mantle during the ''[[Batman: Prodigal|Prodigal]]'' storyline before Bruce returned to the role full-time in the ''[[Batman: Troika|Troika]]'' storyline. He would later take on the mantle on a more permanent basis following Bruce's "death" in ''[[Final Crisis]]'' until ''[[Flash: Flashpoint|Flashpoint]]''.
* '''[[James Gordon|Commissioner James Gordon]]''' of the [[Gotham City Police Department]], who took on the mantle following Bruce's disappearance after the ''[[Batman: Endgame|Endgame]]'' storyline and used [[Rookie (battlesuit)|Rookie]], a mecha Bat-suit, to fight crime.
* '''[[Timothy Fox|Jace Fox]]''', the outcast son of [[Lucius Fox]] who became the Batman of New York.

''Batman'' was created by writer [[Bill Finger]] and artist [[Bob Kane]], first appearing in {{c|Detective Comics Vol 1 27}} ([[1939]]). Since then, Batman has been one of the most well-known [[DC Comics]] characters alongside [[Superman]] and [[Wonder Woman]] throughout his entire comics [[Batman Publication History|publication history]] and also in [[:Category:Other Media|other media]]. This also extends to both his [[Batman Family|supporting cast]] and his [[Batman Villains|rogues gallery]], particularly his arch-enemy the [[Joker]].

